## Bug Analysis

The error `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'city')` means `order.shipping_address` is `undefined` at runtime. You're trying to access `.city` on `undefined`.

**Why it works locally:** Your test data always has a complete `shipping_address` object. In production, some orders likely have a missing or `null` `shipping_address` (e.g., digital orders, incomplete checkout data, or an upstream API omitting the field).

**The fix:** Use optional chaining so that a missing `shipping_address` gracefully falls through to the `"standard"` zone instead of crashing.

<solution language="javascript" verdict="fix">
function getShippingZone(order) {
    const city = order.shipping_address?.city;
    const zones = {
        "New York": "east",
        "Los Angeles": "west",
        "Chicago": "central",
    };
    return zones[city] || "standard";
}
</solution>

### What changed

| Before | After | Why |
|--------|-------|-----|
| `order.shipping_address.city` | `order.shipping_address?.city` | Returns `undefined` instead of throwing when `shipping_address` is missing |

Now if `shipping_address` is absent, `city` becomes `undefined`, `zones[undefined]` is `undefined`, and the function safely returns `"standard"`.

